{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\f0\fs24 How to Report an Issue with an Agreed Seed Order: A Reseller Checklist \u183? Questions and answers\par A seed order that has already been agreed can still run into problems, and the way those problems are reported makes a real difference to how quickly they can be resolved. A reseller who sends a vague message without references often triggers a slow exchange of clarifying emails. This guide sets out a simple structure for reporting an issue with an agreed seed order so that the supplier can match the message to the right transaction, the exact item and, where possible, the batch. It also covers the practical point many people overlook: nothing should be shipped back until the return address and procedure have been confirmed.\par \b Why a structured complaint matters\b0\par The most useful complaint connects the issue to the correct transaction, the exact item and, when available, the batch. Missing references force the supplier to ask questions before any investigation can begin, which delays the outcome. A complete message does the opposite: it gives the supplier enough information to identify the agreed order and the relevant seed line without unnecessary back-and-forth. For resellers, the practical benefit is a clear next step rather than a long email thread.\par \b Start with the order or quotation reference\b0\par Every complaint should open with the order reference. If the issue relates to a quotation rather than an order already recorded, use the relevant quotation reference instead. Copy the reference exactly as it appears in the order or quotation documentation so the message can be linked to the correct transaction. Keep this transaction reference separate from the product details. If several seed lines appear under one order, state clearly that the complaint concerns only one of them, and identify that line in the next part of the message.\par \b Identify the exact item and batch\b0\par For a product complaint, include the item reference and the batch reference if it is available. Each reference serves a different purpose: the order or quotation reference identifies the transaction, the item reference identifies the seed concerned, and the batch reference connects the issue to the relevant batch. Use the same item identifier that appears in the order or catalogue records. Where an individual seed reference is distinguished by a cultivar or SKU, include that identifier too. Do not replace the exact item with only a broad crop or species description, and do not guess a batch reference if none is available.\par \b Describe the issue clearly\b0\par After the references, state which item the issue affects and explain what is wrong. A specific description such as \u8220?The issue concerns [item reference], batch [batch reference]\u8221? is more useful than a general statement that there is a problem with the seeds. If the message covers more than one order line, list each item and its reference separately. Keep the description focused on what can be established from the records and the product. If something cannot be confirmed, label it as unconfirmed rather than assuming a cause or another product detail. This separates known facts from the points that still need checking.\par \b Confirm the return address before sending goods\b0\par Do not send goods back simply because the complaint has been written. Before any return, contact the supplier so the return address and procedure can be clarified, and ask for both in the same message that reports the issue. This means a return starts from confirmed instructions rather than an assumed address. Any return or refund is handled under the agreed supply terms and applicable law, and complaint guidance does not limit statutory rights. Check those terms before agreeing on the next step, and use the current for the applicable contact route and guidance.\par \b A simple message format and final check\b0\par A short template keeps the message complete. Use a subject line such as \u8220?Issue with agreed seed order \u8212? [order or quotation reference]\u8221?, then state the order or quotation reference, the exact item reference, the batch reference if available, and a specific description of the issue. Add a line asking for the return address and procedure to be confirmed before any goods are sent back, and ask how the issue should be handled under the agreed supply terms. Before sending, confirm that all applicable details are present: the order or quotation reference, the exact item reference used for the order, the batch reference where available, a clear description of the issue, and the request for return instructions, together with confirmation that no goods will be sent back until those instructions are received.\par {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://bulkseedsinternationalen.wordpress.com/2026/10/27/report-issue-agreed-seed-order-reseller-checklist/"}{\fldrslt How to Report an Issue with an Agreed Seed Order: A Reseller Checklist}}\par {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://bulk-seeds-international.github.io/bulkseedsinternational-en/dateien/minimax-99fee4e0886a559074ea7555/inhalt.odt"}{\fldrslt Related document}}\par }